Context cancellation: sleep returns ctx.Err() wrapped "retry: interrupted: %w"; ctx.Err is a dynamic call.
Go semantics: context.Canceled and context.DeadlineExceeded behind the errorf. (*context.cancelCtx).Err loads the
error from an atomic.Value field, which is out of scope, so expect 1 unresolved(memory) entry behind the errorf
chain (1 of 1 candidates) and nothing unwrapped.
-- args --
retry/retry.go:@sleep
